      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Iona House, a wonderful, unique and spacious period home enjoying outstanding panoramic sea views whilst enjoying the mix of period features with a modern flair.\n\nHaving been lovingly transformed into a well-proportioned home with approx. 191.88 sqm (2,065 sq ft) of accommodation overlooking the open green space and seafront at Newtownsmith, a short stroll to Dun Laoghaire's East Pier, Sandycove and the Forty Foot bathing facility as well as Glasthule with its wine bars, boutiques, restaurants and artisan shops selling a wide and varied produce.\n\nSandycove & Glasthule Dart Station is close by as are supermarkets in Dun Laoghaire with a cinema, theatre and much, much more all on the doorstep.\n\nThe People's Park which hosts a weekly market is only minutes away as is the famous Teddy's Ice Cream shop.\nThere are a number of schools both Primary and Secondary within easy reach, some of these include Castle Park School, The Harold School, Loreto Dalkey, Holy Child Killiney, St Joseph of Cluny, Rathdown School, CBC Monkstown Park, Blackrock College and St Andrew's College to name only a few so easily accessible to this home.\n\nAccommodation consists of a sitting-room to the front with utility room at this level. There is a hidden door to the bedroom wing which is on the ground floor with three spacious bedrooms, the main bedroom suite includes an ensuite shower room. There is a luxuriously fitted family bathroom at this level.\n\nWithin the sitting-room there is a modern staircase to the first allow return with a shower room. Also, at this level there is the open plan kitchen, breakfast room and family room which opens to the private lawned garden approximately 20m long which enjoys a sunny south westerly aspect.\n\nFrom the first floor return the staircase leads to the dining-room which enjoys elevated sea views. There is also a study at this level.\n\nFloor area approx. : 191.88 sq m (2,065 sq ft)\n\nOutstanding sea views\n\nOn street carparking with resident's disk parking permits \n\nOutstanding period features with modern flair\n\nSpacious bedrooms with main bedroom ensuite\n\nPrivate, secure rear garden approx. 20m long enjoying a sunny south westerly aspect\n\nLocated close to Glasthule, Dun Laoghaire & Sandycove\n\nA short walk to Sandycove & Glasthule Dart Station\n\nAccommodation\n\nEntrance porch: 1.89 m x 1.29 m with glass panelled door to\n\nSitting room: 6.09 m x 4.66 m with feature fireplace with painted mantle and hearth, fitted shelving, hidden door to bedroom corridor, feature staircase to upper floors and opening to\n\nLobby: with store cupboard and door to\n\nUtility room: 2.81 m x 1.77 m plumbed for washing machine with hot press\n\nBedroom wing hallway: 1.35 m x 10.78 m\n\nFamily bathroom 3.89 m x 2.37 m with tiled floor, wc, wash basin, shower with tile surround, bath and heated towel rail\n\nBedroom 1: 3.62 m x 3.78 m with double doors to side, fitted wardrobe and drawer unit with fitted desk\n\nBedroom 2: 3.79 m x 3.81 m with double doors to side fitted shelving and desk unit\n\nBedroom 3: 3.81 m x 4.73 m overall with double doors to side and\n\nEnsuite shower room: with shower, wc and wash basin with tiling\n\n Staircase from sitting room to first floor return\n\nLobby: 3.3 m x 1.17 m with door to\n\nShower room: with shower, wc, wash basin, tiled floor and tiled walls.\n\nOpen plan kitchen/breakfast room/family room: 4.8 m x 11.26 m comprising\n\nKitchen: with tiled floor, range of fitted cupboards, presses and marble worksurface, Electrolux oven, Zanussi microwave, four ring hob, Liebherr fridge, and fitted cupboards\n\nBreakfast & family room: with feature glazed windows and door to rear garden.\n\nStaircase from return to\n\nDining room: 2.05 m x 3.85 m with bay window enjoying views of Sandycove, the sea, Newtownsmith and the East Pier with door to\n\nStudy: 2.14 m x 4.66 m with window overlooking the sea\n\nExternal:\n\nOff the kitchen, breakfast and family room there is a very attractive sun deck leading to the garden.\n\nThe garden which faces south west is laid out in lawn with granite wall and lawns and shrubbed garden and measures approx. 20m \n\nTo the front there is a railed garden with on street carparking with residential disk parking."
